links
Usage: links [-dump] URL_or_FILE

A text-mode web browser: it renders html/http with no gui, so you can read a
served zim, browse a local page, or view a site over a tunnel from the console.
`-dump` prints a page as text and exits, for scripting.

	links URL          browse interactively (q to quit)
	links -dump URL    render the page to stdout and exit
	links file.html    open a local file

See also: kiwix-serve, mutool, httpx
